.SH "NAME"
pcre2_serialize_free \- free serialized compiled patterns
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBvoid\fP pcre2_serialize_free(\fBuint8_t\fP *\fIbytes\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function frees the memory that was obtained by
pcre2_serialize_encode() to hold a serialized byte stream. The argument
must point to such a byte stream or be \f(CRNULL\fP, in which case the function returns
without doing anything.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the serialization functions in the
\f(CRpcre2serialize\fP
page.